# Party production deployment — the one value the owner fills in.
#
# Copy this file to services/party/ops/production.env and set PARTY_DOMAIN to
# the hostname that will serve BOTH the static controller pages and the /api/
# surface. tools/deploy_party.sh threads it into the Wrangler custom-domain
# route and into PARTY_ORIGIN, so the two can never disagree.
#
#   cp services/party/ops/production.env.example services/party/ops/production.env
#   $EDITOR services/party/ops/production.env
#
# Requirements:
#   * a bare hostname — no scheme, no port, no path, no trailing dot
#   * a host on a zone in the same Cloudflare account as the Worker, because a
#     custom-domain route provisions the certificate for it
#   * NOT a *.workers.dev host: phones load this over TLS from a QR code and
#     the launcher's compiled MDKR_PARTY_ORIGIN must match it exactly
#
# production.env is untracked. It holds no secret — PARTY_HMAC_KEY and
# OPS_READ_TOKEN live only in the Wrangler secret store, never in this file.
PARTY_DOMAIN=
